%
% @disclaimer:
%
% This file is not a drop-in-replacement for prettytex/base from the main branch of the project, as package
% options are now handled via xkveyval. Furthermore, the colouring of operators was removed.
%
% @notes:
%
% This packages hase a few macros which are preceded by `prettytexMath`, these are used to make symbols like Hom,
% dim or deg more modular. These macros are always referred to by just the part after `prettytexMath`, i.e.
% when you read `Endomorphisms` in reference to a macro, it actually refers to `prettytexMathEndomorphisms`. This is
% heavily used in the tables where these macros are defined. To avoid any confusion, prettytexMath-macros are always
% listed separately, see e.g. the sections on Topology or Algebra.
% 
% This split is done to ensure all things that are MathOperators can easily be changed by just
% redefining the corresponding prettytexMath macro, for example, if we wish to change our notation for the range
% from `ran` to `range`, instead of redefining the MathOperator `\range`, we simply redefine `Range` to `range` as
% such:
%
%       \renewcommand{\prettytexMathRange}{range}
% 
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ProvidesPackage{prettytex/math}
\RequirePackage{prettytex/base}
\RequirePackage{xparse}

