% BEHOLD, the most over the top subsection
%
% prettytexMath:
% 
% | macro                  | expands to |
% |------------------------|------------|
% | Transpose              | \mathsf{t} |
% | HermitianTranspose     | \mathsf{H} |
% | Trace                  | trace      |
% | Rank                   | rank       |
% | RowRank                | rank       |
% | ColumnRank             | rank       |
% | DotProductPlaceholder  | \cdot      |
% | NormPlaceholder        | \cdot      |
% | Dimension              | dim        |
% | LinearSpan             | span       |
% | GeneralLinearGroup     | GL         |
% | SpecialLinearGroup     | SL         |
% | SpecialUnitaryGroup    | SU         |
% | SpecialOrthogonalGroup | SO         |
% | LpDefaultExponent      | p          |
% | Diagonal               | diag       |
% | Eigen                  | Eig        |
% | Gram                   | Gram       |
% | Spectrum               | spec       |
% | Annihilator            | Ann        |
% | AdjugateMatrix         | Adj        |
% | CofactorMatrix         | Cof        |
%
% macros:
% 
% e is an abbreviation for expression
% O means the argument is optional and has a defalt value
% o means the argument is optional
%
% | macro   | arguments               | description |
% |------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
% | tran    |                         | transpose of a matrix (use like A\tran in math mode)                         |
% | itran   |                         | inverse transpose of a matrix                                                |
% | htran   |                         | hermitian transpose of a matrix                                              |
% | vec     | expression              | element of a vectorspace (typically reserved for coordinate vectors)         |
% | hvec    | expression              | vector with hat                                                              |
% | whvec   | expression              | vector with widehat                                                          |
% | tvec    | expression              | vector with tilde                                                            |
% | wtvec   | expression              | vector with widetilde                                                        |
% | bvec    | expression              | vector with bar                                                              |
% | uvec    | expression              | vector with ubar                                                             |
% | zvec    |                         | zero vector                                                                  |
% | mat     | expression              | matrix (mathrms the argument)                                                |
% | hmat    | expression              | matrix with hat                                                              |
% | whmat   | expression              | matrix with widehat                                                          |
% | tmat    | expression              | matrix with tilde                                                            |
% | wtmat   | expression              | matrix with widetilde                                                        |
% | barmat  | expression              | matrix with bar                                                              |
% | ubarmat | expression              | matrix with ubar                                                             |
% | bmat    | arraystretch (o), array | writes a bmatrix with the supplied array                                     |
% | fbmat   | array                   | writes a bNiceMatrix with the supplied array                                 |
% | detm    | array                   | array notation for a determinant (i.e. with just vertical lines as delims)   |
% | dotp    | expression, expression  | dot product of #1 and #2, delimited with langle and rangle                   |
% | ldotp   | expression, expression  | same as dotp, but with scaling delimiters                                    |
% | dotpc   |                         | dot-product of placeholders (used for function definition, see doc for more) |
% | Lpdotp  | p (O), space (o), e, e  | Lp-dot-product of the two expressions/functions first optional argument      |
% |         |                         | defaults to LpDefaultExponent and is the exponent of the Lp-space,           |
% |         |                         | second argument can be used to specify the measure/measurable space          |
% | lLpdotp | p (O), space (o), e, e  | same as Lpdotp, but with automatically scaling delimiters                    |
% | Lpdotc  | p (O), space (o)        | Lp-dot product of placeholders (used for definition)                         |
% |         |                         | optional parameters work like in Lpdotp                                      |
% | norm    | expression              | norm of the expression (used || for delimiters)                              |
% | lnorm   | expression              | same as norm, but with automatically scaling delimiters                      |
% | normc   |                         | norm of placeholder, used for definition, see docs                           |
% | inorm   | expression              | infinity norm of expression, norm with subscript \infty afterwards           |
% | linorm  | expression              | same as inorm, but with automatically scaling delimiters                     |
% | inormc  |                         | infinity-norm of placeholder, used for definition                            |
% | pnorm   | p (O), expression       | p-norm of expression, p is optionals and defaults to LpDefaultExponent       |
% | lpnorm  | p (O), expression       | same as pnorm, but with automatically scaling delimiters                     |
% | pnormc  | p (O)                   | pnorm of placeholder, see docs for more                                      |
% | Lpnorm  | p (O), space (o), e     | Lp-norm of expression, p is optional and defaults to LpDefaultExponent       |
% |         |                         | space is optional and used to specify the measure/measurable space           |
% | lLpnorm | p (O), space (o), e     | same as Lpnorm but with automatically scaling delimiters                     |
% | Lpnormc | p (O), space (o)        | Lp-norm of placeholder, optional arguments work like in Lpnorm               |
%
% Operators:
%
% | operator | description                                                   |
% |----------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
% | lspan    | linear span of collection of vectors                          |
% | dim      | dimension of space                                            |
% | GL       | general linear group                                          |
% | SL       | special linear group                                          |
% | SU       | special unitary group                                         |
% | SO       | special orthogonal group                                      |
% | diag     | diagonal-matrix from elements or diagonal of a matrix         |
% | Eig      | eigendata (i.e. values and vectors) of an operator            |
% | Gram     | Gram matrix                                                   |
% | spec     | spectrum of operator                                          | 
% | Ann      | annihilator of object                                         |
% | Adj      | Adjugate matrix (NOT the adjoint)                             |
% | Cof      | cofactor matrix                                               |
% | trace    | trace of operator (for a matrix: sum of diagonal entries)     |
% | Trace    | alias for trace                                               |
% | tr       | alias for trace                                               |
% | Tr       | alias for trace                                               |
% | spur     | alias for trace (german spelling)                             |
% | Spur     | alias for trace (german spelling)                             |
% | spr      | alias for trace (german spelling)                             |
% | Spr      | alias for trace (german spelling)                             |
% | rank     | rank of operator (dimension of image)                         |
% | Rank     | alias for rank                                                |
% | rk       | alias for rank                                                |
% | Rk       | alias for rank                                                |
% | rang     | alias for rank (german spelling)                              |
% | Rang     | alias for rank (german spelling)                              |
% | rg       | alias for rank (german spelling)                              |
% | Rg       | alias for rank (german spelling)                              |
% | rowrank  | row rank of matrix (dimension of space spanned by rows)       |
% | rrk      | alias for rowrank                                             |
% | zrg      | alias for rowrank (german spelling)                           |
% | Zrg      | alias for rowrank (german spelling)                           |
% | colrank  | column rank of matrix (dimension of space spanned by columns) |
% | crk      | alias for colrank                                             |
% | srg      | alias for colrank (german spelling)                           |
% | Srg      | alias for colrank (german spelling)                           |
%
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\let\arrvec\vec

